{"major_step_id":3,"reasoning_of_major_step":"The student has not yet performed the summation over all subsets S of B to obtain the total number of ordered pairs.  They stated they would "summarize how to count the total" but did not write the sum or simplify it to 3^b 2^{2^n−b−1}.  Thus step 3, which requires carrying out that sum, is incomplete.","confidence_of_major_step":5,"hint_id":"3.1","reasoning_of_hint":"The student needs to explicitly set up the sum over all S⊆B and rewrite it in terms of the size of S.  The first substep of step 3 provides exactly this instruction.","confidence_of_hint":5,"hint":"Write the total as a sum over all subsets S of B:

 ∑_{S⊆B} 2^{\,|P(A)|−|S|−1}

and then rewrite this sum by letting k=|S|:

 ∑_{k=0}^{b}  inom{b}{k} 2^{\,2^{n}−k−1}."}
